<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.8.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00194</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.8.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0b6933f3-a081-4c2e-bd23-abee2946eeba</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>

<para>For 1 - 4 use the problem below:</para>


<para><quote>Priya is buying raisins and almonds to make trail mix. Almonds cost $5.20 per pound and raisins cost $2.75 per
  pound. Priya spent $11.70 buying almonds and raisins. The relationship between pounds of almonds, pounds of
    raisins, and the total cost is represented by the equation \(5.2a+2.75r=11.7\).</quote></para><section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="141ee309-47d6-4ef8-a902-faf57beecc60" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>How many pounds of raisins did Priya buy if she bought the following amount of almonds:</para><para>2 pounds of almonds</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>1.192</para><para>2.75</para><para>0.946</para><para>0.473</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! 0.473</para><para>\(5.2(2) + 2.75r = 11.7\)
        \(10.4 + 2.75r = 11.7\)
        \(10.4 + 2.75r - 10.4 = 11.7 - 10.4\)
        \(2.75r = 1.3\)
        \((1/2.75) (2.75r) = (1/2.75) (1.3)\)
        \(r = 0.473\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2. </para><para>The correct answer is 0.473. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="aa71602e-9229-4eea-a6a2-8eb5dfac8752" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>1.06 pounds of almonds</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>2.25</para><para>1.689</para><para>5.5</para><para>2.811</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! 2.25 </para><para>\(5.2(1.06) + 2.75r = 11.7\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2. </para><para>The correct answer is 2.25. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="2ecb1097-cef5-424f-938a-28c3ab6edf15" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>0.64 pounds of almonds</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>9.94</para><para>1.911</para><para>3.044</para><para>8.371</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! 3.044</para><para>\(5.2(0.64) + 2.75r = 11.7\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2. </para><para>The correct answer is 3.044. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="04e4c308-5efd-4fe9-b71d-e10a46997b05" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(a\) pounds of almonds</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(r=\frac{11.7+5.2a}{275}\)</para><para>\(r=\frac{11.7-2.75a}{5.2}\)</para><para>\(r=\frac{2.75}{11.7-5.2a}\)</para><para>\(r=\frac{11.7-5.2a}{2.75}\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(r=\frac{1.7-5.2a}{2.75}\)</para><para>\(5.2(a) + 2.75r = 11.7\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2. </para><para>The correct answer is \(r=\frac{11.7-5.2a}{2.75}\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="b5b4af86-a741-4892-a2a9-94abd8e233ed" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For 5 - 6 use the problem below:</para><para><quote>A car traveled 180 miles at a constant rate.</quote></para><para> For each of the missing spaces in the table, a-d, select the missing value that
          completes the table to show the rate at which the car was traveling if it
          completed the same distance in each number of hours.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              Travel Time(Hours)
            </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
              Rate of Travel(Miles Per Hour)
            </emphasis></entry></row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>5</entry>
            <entry>a. ____ </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>4.5</entry>
            <entry>b. ____ </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>3</entry>
            <entry>c. ____ </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>2.25</entry>
            <entry>d. ____ </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <para>   a.______</para>
    </problem><solution><para>Correct! 36</para><para>\(\frac{180}{5}=36\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para><para>The correct answer is 36. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="949cd5c8-e172-4c75-9046-f688c03bbaba" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>b. _____</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! 40</para><para>\(\frac{180}{4.5}=40\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para><para>The correct answer is 40. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="ed99f41d-13e6-4be7-b1ba-e786dd1d841c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>c. _____</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! 60</para><para>\(\frac{180}{3}=60\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para><para>The correct answer is 60. </para><para>\(\frac{180}{3}=60\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="e46a957b-f722-4e79-acb0-5917929b9c84" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>d. _____</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! 80</para><para>\(\frac{180}{2.25}=80\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para><para>The correct answer is 80. </para><para>\(\frac{180}{2.25}=80\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="0d45981e-3d0c-4b99-9426-0f75365c3047" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Choose the equation that would make it easy to find the rate at which the car
          was traveling in miles per hour \(r\), if it traveled for \(t\) hours.</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(r=\frac t{180}\)</para><para>\(r=\frac{180}t\)</para><para>\(r=180t\)</para><para>\(r-180-t\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(r=\frac{180}t\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para><para>The correct answer is \(r=\frac{180}t\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="48e38499-b2ca-4eb1-ba5e-2bb72198961b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> Bananas cost $0.50 each, and apples cost $1.00 each. <emphasis>Select all three</emphasis> combinations of bananas
          and apples that Elena could buy for exactly $3.50.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 3 bananas and 2 apples,1 banana and 3 apples, 5 bananas and 1 apple</para><para>\(3(0.5)+2(1)=3.50\)
        \(1(0.5)+3(1)=3.50\)
        \(5(.5)+1(1)=3.50\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2. </para><para>The correct answers are 3 bananas and 2 apples,1 banana and 3 apples, 5 bananas and 1 apple. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="e41358fd-8187-4c65-b531-f0ea183aee73" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Choose the best answer to solve the formula \(A=P+Prt\) for \(t\).</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(t=\frac{P-A}{Pr}\)</para><para>\(t=\frac{A-P}{Pr}\)</para><para>\(t=\frac{A+P}{Pr}\)</para><para>\(t=\frac{r(A-P)}P\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(t=\frac{A-P}{Pr}\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para><para>The correct answer is \(t=\frac{A-P}{Pr}\). </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
